BT /F1 10 Tf 50 720 Td (IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
AT NEW DELHI

CASE NO: Crl.A. No. 102 of 2026
CNR NUMBER: SCIN010012342026
DECISION DATE: 2026-03-05
YEAR: 2026

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Chief Justice of India & Justice B.R. Gavai & Justice Surya Kant

PARTIES:
Vikas Yadav
... Appellant\(s\) / Petitioner\(s\)
Versus
State of Uttar Pradesh
... Respondent\(s\) / State

STATUTORY PROVISIONS & ACTS REFERRED:
Indian Penal Code, Code of Criminal Procedure 1973, Constitution of India

SECTIONS & CLAUSES UNDER CONSIDERATION:
IPC Section 302, CrPC Section 354\(3\), Article 21

KEY LEGAL DOMAINS & TOPICS:
Death Penalty, Rarest of Rare, Commutation, Mitigating Circumstances, Reformation

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTUAL MATRIX:
Convict was sentenced to death for multiple murders. High Court confirmed death sentence. Supreme Court examined psychiatric evaluation and jail conduct records.

2. ISSUES FRAMED FOR ADJUDICATION:
1. Whether possibility of reformation was adequately ruled out before imposing capital punishment?

3. STATUTORY FRAMEWORK & PRECEDENTS:
Manoj v. State of M.P. mandates comprehensive psychological assessment and socioeconomic report of convict before capital sentencing.

4. RATIO DECIDENDI:
Death sentence cannot be confirmed unless prosecution conclusively proves by cogent material that convict is incapable of reformation.

5. FINAL DISPOSITION & ORDER:
Criminal Appeal Partly Allowed; Death sentence commuted to 25 years imprisonment without remission.

Decreed and ordered accordingly.

Hon'ble Chief Justice of India & Justice B.R. Gavai & Justice Surya Kant
Supreme Court of India
